WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:01.939
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.939 --> 00:00:06.779
In the southwest of China's Sichuan province
sits a small village called Atuleer.

00:00:06.779 --> 00:00:13.110
Where the local schoolchildren must climb
an 800 metre bamboo ladder up the side of

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:17.210
a sheer cliff face, just to get to school.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:22.830
The only school for many miles around sits
atop this rocky outcrop, there are no roads

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:26.030
or pathways to the top, only this ladder.

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:32.050
I bet your journey to school seems incredibly
benign in comparison.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:36.930
You may not have to scale a cliff face to
attend school, but the education you receive

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:44.130
every day, or did once receive is just as
precarious and insufficient.

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:46.559
Education is broken.

00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:51.050
Over the past 50 years the world has changed
beyond recognition, yet the school systems,

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:54.579
in most countries have stayed static.

00:00:54.579 --> 00:00:59.920
Our current education systems were designed
and built in the industrial age, in some countries

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:02.520
that's as long ago as the 18th century.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:08.619
Sure there have been many subtle changes over
the decades but the basic goal of our school

00:01:08.619 --> 00:01:14.450
systems has remained exactly the same for
over 200 years.

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:16.229
And what is that goal?

00:01:16.229 --> 00:01:19.869
To produce obedient factory workers.

00:01:19.869 --> 00:01:25.249
During the industrial era and right up to
the epoch of the 21st century, most people

00:01:25.249 --> 00:01:32.139
worked in manufacturing, either on production
lines, on farms or in mines.

00:01:32.139 --> 00:01:38.560
Where things like creativity and individuality
only get in the way of profits.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:43.979
Factory owners needed obedient drones in large
numbers and so many wealthy business owners

00:01:43.979 --> 00:01:50.060
invested large sums of money into lobbying,
to influence politicians to shape the school

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:54.119
systems in the ideologies of said factory
owners.

00:01:54.119 --> 00:01:59.880
Putting values such as order and discipline
as top priority and making sure that creativity

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:02.989
and individualism were quashed.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:08.330
Such lobbying happened mostly in America but
nevertheless, the school systems in most developed

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:14.270
countries today are still built on the same
robotic and stale ideologies.

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:20.250
And so kids today arrive at school nice and
early, not a minute too late.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:25.530
We are ordered to sit down in our pre-designated
seats, because god only knows what utter chaos

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:28.690
would unravel if we were to sit where we pleased.

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:33.990
We are programmed to respond to a series of
bells and whistles that signify when we are

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:36.820
allowed to eat and leave.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:41.990
We have to ask permission to speak, to move,
to go to the bathroom.

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:48.730
This used to be kind of okay, because this
forced obedience would carry over to the factory

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:53.240
floor, which is where most people ended up,
right after school.

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:59.620
But today, and for quite some time now, we
have been living in a world where most people

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:04.810
can do whatever they desire for a career if
they try hard enough.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:13.120
I mean you can actually be a professional
bed warmer, a pet food taster or a Ravenmaster,

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.860
yes these are all real jobs.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:21.470
The nature of jobs has changed drastically
and today we live in a world where qualities

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:29.710
such as creativity, individualism and entrepreneurialism
are highly sought after by a lot of employers.

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:35.840
Let me ask you a question, how come, if you're
bad at English, Maths or Science you're repeatedly

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.080
told "you're not trying hard enough".

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:43.260
Your work is scrutinised, your parents are
notified of your "poor performance", you're

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:47.790
made to re-sit tests until you get it right.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:55.690
Yet if you're bad at art, music or sport you're
simply told "don't worry, it's just not you're

00:03:55.690 --> 00:04:01.380
thing" despite these all being entirely valid
career choices.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:07.530
The huge fact of life that modern school systems
ignore is that everyone has their own unique

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:11.030
talents and things they are really passionate
about.

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:17.340
We're all naturally good at something and
terrible at other things, whether that's because

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.859
of our genetics or upbringing.

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:26.800
Some children are more creative whilst others
are more academic; we're all unique.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:31.879
Albert Einstein supposedly wrote "Everybody
is a genius.

00:04:31.879 --> 00:04:36.449
But if you judge a fish by its ability to
climb a tree, it will live its whole life

00:04:36.449 --> 00:04:39.300
believing that it is stupid."

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:43.800
The human brain's ability and desire to learn
is astonishing.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:50.430
And yes it is possible for almost anyone to
learn anything, I'm not saying that every

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:54.870
child shouldn't learn mathematics because
every child can.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:05:01.349
But where most school systems fail is in bringing
out the best in every child and encouraging

00:05:01.349 --> 00:05:04.500
exploration of their natural abilities.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:11.080
But the really stupid thing is that schools
don't even do a decent job of teaching English,

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:16.250
Maths and Science, in fact they do a rather
terrible job indeed.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:21.770
Public education today is based on a system
of taking a bunch of information and systematically

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:24.710
reciting that information to the students.

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:28.879
Whom are later tested on their ability to
remember this information.

00:05:28.879 --> 00:05:35.090
And the key point here is that exams only
test a child's ability to remember.

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:40.919
So weeks before your exam you would recite
the same textbook information over and over

00:05:40.919 --> 00:05:46.080
again until you had near enough, the entire
textbook memorised.

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:49.819
But what happens after the exam?

00:05:49.819 --> 00:05:51.940
You forget it all.

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:58.969
Multiple studies have shown that children
and adults forget 95% of everything they learn

00:05:58.969 --> 00:06:02.490
via memorisation, after just three days.

00:06:02.490 --> 00:06:09.750
So an A* test score says no more about a child
than their ability to recite information,

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:16.509
it is not a strongly correlated representation
of actual intelligence, that is the ability

00:06:16.509 --> 00:06:20.199
to acquire new skills by one's own accord.

00:06:20.199 --> 00:06:26.770
This process of faux learning via memorisation
is known as inauthentic learning, because

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:32.419
you aren't actually learning, only regurgitating
information.

00:06:32.419 --> 00:06:35.770
Anyone can do that, it's what I do for a living.

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:40.039
So you ask, how does one learn authentically?

00:06:40.039 --> 00:06:44.490
How do we actually teach kids instead of asking
them to memorise?

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:49.650
Well, we quite simply have to spark their
curiosity.

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:54.990
Humans are unquenchably curious, as toddlers
we have to touch everything we see, stick

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:58.569
our fingers in plug sockets and dismantle
everything.

00:06:58.569 --> 00:07:03.680
That curiosity never leaves us, it's hopefully
why you watch my videos.

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:09.499
When you allow children to become curious
about something they will actually teach themselves

00:07:09.499 --> 00:07:13.840
because they have a primal desire to find
out as much as they can.

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:21.680
And the best part is that this self-curiosity-driven
learning is completely authentic and children

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:27.839
will absorb that knowledge like a sponge and
most importantly, you can be sure they will

00:07:27.839 --> 00:07:33.550
remember it, because when we are engaged we
are happy and our brains naturally remember

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:35.789
the times when we are happy.

00:07:35.789 --> 00:07:42.550
A great number of the world's greatest thinkers,
its greatest entrepreneurs and history's greatest

00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:48.669
leaders all share something in common, they
dropped out of school.

