00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:10.820
Now, there's another fundamental problem with
school today and it's not to do with what

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:12.630
goes on in the classroom.

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:15.520
I'm talking about sleep.

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:20.080
When you start a job it's generally accepted
that you will turn up at 9am or earlier every

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:26.420
morning and this same time expectation is
put upon school kids all the way from primary

00:11:26.420 --> 00:11:28.800
school, to high-school, college and university.

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:34.600
But there's a deep-rooted biological issue
with that, which explains why when I was at

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:39.170
school I spent at least 30% of my lessons
asleep at my desk.

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:43.640
Our bodies are phenomenal time keepers, and
our subconscious is often well aware of the

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:47.790
current time, even if your conscious mind
isn't.

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:52.290
You know how sometimes you wake up exactly
one minute before your alarm clock.

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:55.780
This is because of your body's circadian rhythm.

00:11:55.780 --> 00:12:01.230
This is our internal clock and it also determines
when is the best time for us to fall asleep

00:12:01.230 --> 00:12:02.630
and to wake up.

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:05.850
But our circadian rhythm varies throughout
our lives.

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:10.170
When we're younger than 10 our bodies want
to wake up as early as possible but it soon

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:13.700
gets later and later throughout adolescence.

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:19.420
Between the ages of 14 and 24 our circadian
rhythm is set at the latest it will ever be

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:25.140
in our lives and our natural desire is to
wake up later in the morning, for example,

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:26.640
after 10am.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:30.830
There's nothing we can do to fight this urge.

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:37.630
Recent studies have shown that forcing teenage
students to wake up before 7am to attend school

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:43.410
between 8am and 9am plays havoc with our body's
intended sleep cycle.

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:48.380
The result is that teenagers get far less
sleep throughout these critical years and

00:12:48.380 --> 00:12:53.600
concentration in the classroom takes a steep
dive into the sleepy abyss.

00:12:53.600 --> 00:13:00.160
There is absolutely no scientific evidence
that starting school any earlier than 10 or

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:04.670
11am is beneficial to learning, quite the
opposite in fact.

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:07.580
Thankfully this, at least, is changing.

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:12.580
Over the past couple of years in Britain,
as part of large experiment funded by a London

00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:17.240
charity, hundreds of schools across the UK
are being asked to shift their school days

00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:23.170
forward an hour or two and asking students
to arrive at 10am instead.

00:13:23.170 --> 00:13:28.910
This experiment is still ongoing today but
early indications from this large-scale test

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:34.850
have already shown that school children across
the country are happier, more engaged, learning

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:40.430
more and the rising rates of mental illness
among teenagers, which has been partially

00:13:40.430 --> 00:13:45.170
attributed to sleep deprivation, are starting
to plateau.

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:50.670
There is one country that has taken changing
the entire school system into their own hands

00:13:50.670 --> 00:13:58.200
and made changes so sweeping that the way
they "do school" is completely unrecognisable

00:13:58.200 --> 00:13:59.490
to most of us.

00:13:59.490 --> 00:14:06.450
And as a result, this country now has the
most successful school system in the entire

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:07.870
world.

00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:10.780
Welcome to Finland.

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:16.420
Over the years multiple studies have ranked
Finland as the most successful and most efficient

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:18.480
school system in the world.

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:23.690
And they rank #2 globally for science and
#3 for reading.

00:14:23.690 --> 00:14:29.860
But what does Finland do so differently, to
the US for example, which consistently ranks

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:32.950
down in the mid 30s for efficiency?

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:39.300
America also ranks #33 in science and #17
in reading.

00:14:39.300 --> 00:14:43.850
For a start, children in Finland don't even
start school until the age of seven, compared

00:14:43.850 --> 00:14:49.960
to the normal age of five, in most countries,
allowing them far more time to just "be children".

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:57.120
And for the first six years of a child's education
in Finland, they are not measured in any way,

00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:02.890
it literally doesn't matter how they perform
in class, because seriously, what is the point

00:15:02.890 --> 00:15:09.020
in testing a 10 year old when all they really
want to do is paint on walls and lick trees.

00:15:09.020 --> 00:15:16.960
In fact there is only one, just one standardised
test during the entirety of a child's education

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:21.590
in Finland, and it's not taken until they're
16 years old.

00:15:21.590 --> 00:15:26.550
And that exam isn't even a "test" per se,
it's used to find out which students need

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:29.600
more individual help than the others.

00:15:29.600 --> 00:15:34.810
Homework is far less common and they don't
begin to issue homework until students are

00:15:34.810 --> 00:15:37.140
well into their teen years.

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:42.750
In fact Finish kids spend the least time on
homework per week than any country in the

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:48.760
world, at an average of just over 2 hours
per week compared to six hours per week for

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:50.940
the average American pupil.

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:56.440
The Finish school day is far shorter than
other countries, they typically start at 9am

00:15:56.440 --> 00:16:00.210
and finish school between 1 and 2pm.

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:05.570
Teachers in Finland only work for a maximum
of 4 hours each day and they put aside two

00:16:05.570 --> 00:16:11.570
hours each week for professional development,
helping them to be better teachers.

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:16.700
One of the biggest differences between Finish
and American schools is the amount of free-time

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:18.870
students are permitted.

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:25.370
In Finland students get a 15 minute break
after every lesson.

00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:31.660
The average daily break time of a Finish school
student is a whopping 75 minutes, compared

00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:36.020
to just 27 minutes for an American student.

00:16:36.020 --> 00:16:42.270
Recent studies have conclusively shown that
more break time relative to class time, actually

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:48.710
increases test scores and learning, and decreases
mental illness, depression and general bad

00:16:48.710 --> 00:16:51.630
behaviour amongst school children.

00:16:51.630 --> 00:16:58.590
Quite simply a happy and healthy child is
going to be less bored and more engaged.

00:16:58.590 --> 00:17:05.170
So how do Finland do when it comes to encouraging
every child's unique abilities?

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:11.699
Remarkably well actually, Finish school pupils
have 25 lessons a week and nine of these are

00:17:11.699 --> 00:17:14.670
arts, crafts, music and sports.

00:17:14.670 --> 00:17:17.380
That's almost 40% of lessons.

00:17:17.380 --> 00:17:22.870
Also, the national curriculum in Finland is
just a set of broad guidelines, rather than

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:25.900
a strict checklist that has to be adhered
to.

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:31.710
The individual teachers have a lot more power
to tailor their lessons to suit their students.

00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:36.210
Children aren't segregated into different
classes depending on their intelligence or

00:17:36.210 --> 00:17:39.000
historic test scores.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:44.310
Classes are kept small but children that need
extra help are given huge amounts of 1-on-1

00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:49.190
attention to help get them up to speed and
the results show that the gap between the

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:56.540
worst performing kids and the highest performers
in Finland, is the smallest in the world.

00:17:56.540 --> 00:18:02.520
In Finland no child is left behind, but it's
actually true over there, rather than just

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:05.040
an empty political slogan.

00:18:05.040 --> 00:18:13.130
In Finland the high school dropout rate of
students is a tiny 0.4%, in America it is

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:21.520
25%, by far one of the highest in the developed
world.

00:18:21.520 --> 00:18:26.280
America also has one of the largest gaps between
the tests scores of the rich than the poor

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:27.280
in the world.

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:32.190
But a lot of experts argue that you couldn't
simply take the blueprint for the Finish school

00:18:32.190 --> 00:18:39.980
system and implement it overnight in America,
for one major reason, the two countries are

00:18:39.980 --> 00:18:44.850
culturally, economically and socially very,
very different.

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:52.550
For a start the cultural differences are enormous,
in the US 22% of the population are religiously

00:18:52.550 --> 00:18:58.630
unaffiliated, with just 3% categorising themselves
as atheists.

00:18:58.630 --> 00:19:07.340
Whereas in Finland an impressive 60% of the
country are religiously unaffiliated or non-believers

00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:09.260
and 22% are atheists.

00:19:09.260 --> 00:19:14.300
Almost everyone in Finland is middle class,
they have one of the smallest gaps in the

00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:16.900
world between the rich and poor.

00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:22.960
This allows for a stable and consistent, publicly
funded school system across the entire country.

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:29.600
Whereas America has the biggest wealth inequality
of any developed country, in the world.

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:33.880
This creates huge problems with balancing
the school system from state to state and

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:35.390
district to district.

00:19:35.390 --> 00:19:40.480
In America the gap between the quality of
education in poor areas and wealthy areas

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:41.660
is enormous.

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:46.910
To integrate the Finish system into American
schools, the whole economics of the school

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:55.950
system would have to be turned on its head.

00:19:55.950 --> 00:20:01.240
American teachers get paid merit pay, a top
up on their salary if their students perform

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:03.380
well in standardised tests.

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:09.880
Causing teachers to push their students beyond
reasonable levels to achieve higher test scores,

00:20:09.880 --> 00:20:15.250
with no regard to whether they are genuinely
learning.

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:20.800
Merit pay does not exist in Finland.

00:20:20.800 --> 00:20:25.030
Children in Finland, and most countries for
that matter, can go to school without the

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:26.180
fear of violence.

00:20:26.180 --> 00:20:32.300
The statistics show that in the US, 27% of
students have carried a dangerous weapon to

00:20:32.300 --> 00:20:33.350
school.

00:20:33.350 --> 00:20:41.180
10% have carried a gun to school and 40% have
been in a physical fight whilst at school.

00:20:41.180 --> 00:20:45.930
Now I'm not here to endlessly praise Finland
or to point fingers at the American or any

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:47.809
other school system.

00:20:47.809 --> 00:20:56.480
But proper education is so, unbelievably important
to society, as it is, quite literally, our

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:57.480
future.

00:20:57.480 --> 00:21:02.960
The children of today will be the scientists,
doctors, lawyers and politicians of tomorrow.

00:21:02.960 --> 00:21:08.550
Economists predict that improving the education
system in the US would boost the US economy

00:21:08.550 --> 00:21:13.300
by $27 trillion, over the next few decades.

00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:18.130
Similarly in the UK, economists predict that
there is much room for improvement in our

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:25.380
school system too, and doing so would boost
our economy by £3.6 trillion.

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:31.010
Improving education would mean a better, safer
and more sustainable world for everyone.

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:39.290
Yes, we need to take inspiration from Finland,
but we first need to take inspiration from

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:48.700
their attitude towards society and life.

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:55.840
Thanks for watching.

